  "explanation": {
    "short": "At the start of a word, sp and st sound like \"shp\" and \"sht\": Stadt is SHTAT, spät is SHPAYT. ä is like the e in \"bed\", but long in spät. At the end of a word, b, d and g are said p, t and k: Sonntag ends like \"tahk\", Abend like \"bent\".",
    "more": "This \"hardening\" only happens at the end: in the plural Abende the d is soft again. You will hear it, not have to think about it."
  },
